 "method": {
  "line": "MEMBRANE'S OWN LINE (owner ruling 2026-10-18; lib/wavefront/membraneLine.ts): the per-wallet simulator's rule — weightedMembraneLine of the t0 collateral (MEMBRANE_ASSET_LTV, modelled: WETH 0.80, wstETH 0.78, WBTC 0.75, …; DEPLOY_LAUNCH_LTV, the deploy script's own: sUSDS 0.88, syrupUSDC 0.86, scrvUSD 0.86), value-weighted at t0, each asset clamped to its class cap. Legs with no Membrane line are left out of the weighted line; a position with no leg that has one is excluded ('no-membrane-line'). The protocol's line (Aave weighted LT, Morpho LLTV) stays in each row as `line`: it locates t0 and is the published sensitivity 'Membrane at the protocol's line'. The position still enters at the protocol's liquidation (t0); on a lower line it is further past its line there.",
  "liquidity": "LIQUIDITY-CAPPED SALES (owner ruling 2026-10-18; lib/wavefront/liquidity.ts, meta.liquidity): every sale is an order offered to a shared per-(chain, token) book that allows 1.1x (modelled †) the most tokens liquidators absorbed in any rolling 10 minutes of the window, at any minute, in order minute then pid. The order splits across collateral legs pro rata by value; each leg fills against its own book. The unfilled part stays pending: while it is, the timer is idle, the order is re-sized each minute at that minute’s price (never more than pending, never past the borrow cap: back at or under the cap cancels it) and the LTV moves on the collateral still held. A remainder still pending at the grid end is never credited. A position that would have to sell a token with no observed liquidity on its chain is excluded (no-capacity).",
  "comparison": "DEBT REPAID ONLY (owner ruling 2026-10-18): Membrane’s liquidation fee cannot be assumed, so no collateral-seized figure is compared. Real seized (with the Aave protocol fee) stays in each row as provenance."
 },
